    "narrative": "The primary catalyst for Ghost Ride the WHIP\u2019s offensive production today is **Mickey Moniak**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 75.75. His matchup against Sasaki is tailor-made for a breakout, boosted by a significant 14% park factor and an 88% stolen base success rate against the starter\u2019s slow delivery. We are also leaning into **Isaac Paredes** (68.00) and **Josh Naylor** (61.02); **Isaac Paredes** benefits from an elite platoon advantage against Ure\u00f1a, while **Josh Naylor** provides reliable core production in the five-hole. We are also keeping a close eye on **Corbin Carroll**, who remains a priority start at 60.06; despite the 50% SB hold rate of the opposing pitcher, his speed remains vital to our strategy in this high-wind, favorable-park environment.\n\nThe toughest decision of the day involved **Austin Riley**, who finished with a respectable 54.83 score. While he edged out some of our lower-tier starters in raw value, he ultimately landed on the bench due to an suboptimal eighth-spot lineup position and the fact that he was marginally eclipsed by our high-upside plays like **Henry Bolte** (59.58) and **Seiya Suzuki** (57.65). Meanwhile, we are managing significant volatility in our corners and middle infield; **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, and **Henry Bolte** all carry a 42% rain risk that necessitates monitoring as first pitch approaches. Should the skies clear, we expect **Henry Bolte** to capitalize on his lead-off spot against Lugo, but we are prepared to pivot if weather delays condense our game-cap usage.",
